.DS_Store
*.pyc

# Generated by the converters' *_gen.py scripts. ccd.pickle in particular is
# ~500 MB, well over GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, so rebuild it locally
# rather than committing it.
src/alphafold3/constants/converters/*.pickle

# dev-only: the compiled extension and generated data pickles, symlinked from an
# installed build so `PYTHONPATH=src` imports work without reinstalling.
src/alphafold3/cpp*.so
src/alphafold3/constants/converters/*.pickle

# Jupyter leaves these next to whatever it opens.
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# dev/: the port verification harnesses (native oracles, localisation ladders,
# fold gates, benchmarks). The SOURCE is tracked -- it is the only record of how
# every parity number in PARITY.md was produced, and a checkout that cannot
# re-run the gates cannot check a refactor. What is NOT tracked is everything
# they read or write: native activation dumps and captures (.npz), logs, and
# bytecode. Those are hundreds of megabytes, are regenerated by the scripts
# themselves, and depend on native checkpoints and vendor venvs that are not in
# this repo.
dev/**/*.npz
dev/**/*.pt
dev/**/*.pkl
dev/**/*.cif
dev/**/*.pdb
dev/**/*.log
dev/**/__pycache__/
# run_all_parity.sh's output: one log per gate per model plus a summary.tsv.
# Results, not source -- and PARITY.md is where a result becomes a record.
dev/oracles/parity_runs/
